@startuml
title One synchronous COMM, end to end: `{ in(c,y).0 | c!c.0 }` reduces to `{ 0 | 0 }`

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

participant "**source text**\n`{ in(c,y).0 | c!c.0 }`" as SRC #DCFCE7
participant "**parser.rs**\nPratt / WPDA" as PARSE #DBEAFE
participant "**AC matcher**\nPattern::ac(Proc_PPar, ..., rest)" as MATCH #EDE9FE
participant "**Comm rule**\nop 0, label\nPi::rewrite::Comm" as COMM #FCE7F3
participant "**dispatch arm**\ncomm_dispatch_arm" as ARM #FEF3C7
participant "**e-graph**\ndovetail::EGraph" as EG #DBEAFE

SRC -> PARSE : token stream\n`{` `in` `(` `c` `,` `y` `)` `.` `0` `|` `c` `!` `c` `.` `0` `}`
PARSE -> MATCH : ""PPar(HashBag{ PIn(NVar c, Scope(y, PZero)),""\n""              POut(NVar c, NVar c, PZero) })""

note over PARSE
  ""insert_into_ppar"" flattens nested ""PPar"" on the way in, and
  ""HashBag"" is an unordered multiset — so associativity and
  commutativity of parallel composition hold BY CONSTRUCTION and
  need no equation.
end note

group Match the redex — one AcApp pattern, two element patterns, one remainder
  MATCH -> MATCH : element 0: ""Pattern::app(Proc_PIn,""\n""  [var("n"), leaf(BinderArity(1)), var("p")])""
  MATCH -> MATCH : element 1: ""Pattern::app(Proc_POut,""\n""  [var("n"), var("m"), var("q")])""
  MATCH -> MATCH : **non-linear guard**: `n` occurs in BOTH elements,\nso the re-bind check enforces <latex>n \equiv n</latex> by e-class equality
  MATCH -> MATCH : everything unmatched binds to the remainder ""rest""
end

MATCH -> COMM : sigma = { n |-> `c`, p |-> body of the receive,\n            m |-> `c`, q |-> `0`, rest |-> {} }

group Contract — the interaction cut <latex>c?y.P \mid c!m.Q \longrightarrow P\{m/y\} \mid Q</latex>
  COMM -> ARM : fire op 0
  ARM -> EG : gate: is sigma[p] a fold value, sigma[m] in normal form?
  EG --> ARM : yes — extract the 1-best derivation of each
  ARM -> ARM : rebuild the receive body under a **FRESH** binder\n(""Binder(FreeVar::fresh_unnamed())""), then ""unbind""
  ARM -> ARM : ""__reduct = open_body.substitute_name(&b.0, &arg)""\n= <latex>P\{m/y\}</latex>, capture-avoiding by construction
  ARM -> EG : ""instantiate(Pattern::ac(Proc_PPar,""\n""  [var("__comm_reduct"), var("q")], Some("rest")))""
end

EG -> EG : the reduct bag is merged with the redex bag's e-class;\n""resolve_rewrite_justifications"" records the firing
EG -> SRC : report names the rule **""Comm""**

note over ARM, EG #FEF3C7
  The reduct has **TWO** fixed elements because the output
  ""n!m.q"" is SYNCHRONOUS and carries a continuation ""q"".
  ""CommAsync"" is the same lane with ONE fixed element,
  ""[var("__comm_reduct")]"", because ""POutAsync"" has no
  continuation. The lane admits any arity <latex>m \geq 1</latex>: exactly one
  host-computed substitution plus <latex>m-1</latex> sigma-delivered variables.
end note

note over MATCH #FEE2E2
  Fail-closed: a sigma-delivered reduct element may never be a
  binder SCOPE. Splicing a raw binder body into the reduct
  would let the bound name escape its restriction.
end note

@enduml
